# Review: enum COUNT

The coding standard (`.cursor/rules/xcsoar-project-rules.mdc`, Enums
with Count Values) requires a `COUNT` sentinel and a `static_assert`
on every table that copies the enum.

## Reject

- A new or copied table of an enum's values or display labels with no
  `static_assert` against that enum's `COUNT`
- An enum used from more than one file that has no `COUNT` sentinel

```cpp
// BAD: a second label list the compiler cannot check
static const char *const names[] = { N_("A"), N_("B") };

// GOOD
static_assert(ARRAY_SIZE(names) == unsigned(MyEnum::COUNT));
```
